,title,link,text,language,family
0,Trans–New Guinea languages - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trans–New_Guinea_languages,"Trans–New Guinea (TNG) is an extensive family of Papuan languages spoken on the island of New Guinea and neighboring islands, a region corresponding to the country Papua New Guinea as well as parts of Indonesia.",Fulumu,Trans-New Guinea
1,Music of Papua New Guinea - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Papua_New_Guinea,"The music of Papua New Guinea encompasses a wide range of traditional and contemporary styles developed across the country's highly diverse ethnic groups. Traditional celebrations known as sing-sing feature communal song and dance, and form a central part of cultural life.",Fulumu,Trans-New Guinea
2,Music of Papua New Guinea - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Papua_New_Guinea,"The music of Papua New Guinea encompasses a wide range of traditional and contemporary styles developed across the country's highly diverse ethnic groups. Traditional celebrations known as sing-sing feature communal song and dance, and form a central part of cultural life.",Fulumu,Trans-New Guinea
3,"Fulumu Language (BBD) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/bbd/,"Fulumu is an endangered indigenous language of Papua New Guinea. It belongs to the Trans-New Guinea language family. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people. It is not known to be taught in schools.",Fulumu,Trans-New Guinea
4,Papua New Guinea Traditional Songs (1 Hour Compilation) Tribal Music ...,https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=Z05H4u8ZXNY,“Papua New Guinea” appears here for discoverability. Listening tips • Headphones recommended to feel the low drone & spatial detail. • Best at low–medium volume.,Fulumu,Trans-New Guinea
5,Fula songs mix - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLUmiOA7-LCthB4ICe0opqrds6itHyuJqk,"Listen to Fula songs mix on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more.",Fulumu,Trans-New Guinea
6,Bau in Papua New Guinea people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/10731/PP,"Learn about the Bau in Papua New Guinea people group. Profiles include statistics, text, photo, map, progress indicator and language resources.",Fulumu,Trans-New Guinea
7,Music of Melanesia — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/music_of_melanesia,"The music of Melanesia encompasses the diverse traditional and contemporary musical practices of the indigenous peoples across the island chains of Papua New Guinea, the Solomon Islands, Vanuatu, Fiji, and New Caledonia, regions marked by over 1,100 languages and profound cultural variation. [1] [2] Rooted in kin-based reciprocity and social reproduction, it features intricate vocal styles ...",Fulumu,Trans-New Guinea
8,Fulumu language resources | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/languages/bbd,Fulumu language resources. Listing of people groups speaking Fulumu. Fulumu dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability.,Fulumu,Trans-New Guinea
9,Papuan Folk Music - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/papuan-folk-music,"Papuan folk music refers to the traditional and community-based music of the Indigenous peoples of the island of New Guinea, spanning today’s Papua New Guinea and the Indonesian provinces of Papua and West Papua. It encompasses hundreds of distinct musical micro-traditions tied to language groups, clans, and ecological zones from coastal islands to highland valleys.",Fulumu,Trans-New Guinea
